{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The governing measurement of this trip is the GPS trace, not the rounded trip-record copy. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the field the threshold test runs on, and it records 23.79 km; trip_record.actual_distance_km of 23.8 km is a rounded convenience copy that may not be cited for the threshold test. Against the booked optimal of 18.3 km, the excess actually driven is 5.49 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both limbs of the establishment test in POL-RD-01 pass and pass comfortably. The excess is 30.0% of the optimal route, above the 20% limb, and 5.49 km in absolute terms, above the 0.8 km limb. A route deviation is therefore ESTABLISHED on this trip's own telemetry.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is clean and no gap-handling discount applies. It carries 187 fixes at a 10 second sample interval across the whole 31 minute trip, 100.0% coverage, an empty gaps array and a max_gap_sec of 0.0. None of limbs (a) to (c) of POL-RD-07 is met, so the deviation stands on the trace alone and the corroboration requirement in POL-RD-07(ii) is not engaged, nor is the escalation in POL-RD-10(3).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider has discharged the initial burden under POL-RD-08. Limb (a): the trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip identifier TRP-02856, and the trip_record start time of 15:32:19 matches the trace's first fix at 15:32:19. Limb (b): an excess of 5.49 km and 30.0%, measured from a trace that is unimpaired on any limb of POL-RD-07. The burden has shifted to the driver to point to a specific artifact and a specific clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02856", "EV-GPS-02856", "EV-FARE-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's only excuse is the IMM instruction, and the trace destroys it. The rider's message does name a resolved waypoint, but the nearest the vehicle ever came to the IMM waypoint was 3,088.34 metres, at fix index 90 at 15:47:19. Under POL-RD-04 the corroboration test is that the vehicle passes within 200 m of the requested waypoint or travels the requested road; it did neither, and the derived waypoint_approach block records within_threshold as false. Under POL-RD-14 the instruction therefore did not cause the measured excess: POL-RD-04 does not apply, no distance is excluded, and the deviation is decided under POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 on the trace as measured.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02856", "EV-GPS-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-14", "POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's one-word reply 'ok' does not rescue the excuse. POL-RD-04 corroboration is geographic, not conversational: the clause requires that the gps_trace show the vehicle within 200 m of the waypoint, and the chat log is the very artifact that supplies the waypoint_hint the test is run against. A message that says 'ok' to a stop the vehicle never approached is a reply to a request, not evidence that the request was performed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02856", "EV-GPS-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not the contradiction POL-RD-10(7) describes, and the case does not escalate on it. A request that was made and a route that did not follow it are consistent facts, not mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength. POL-RD-14 states that the driver's reliance on the uncorroborated request is an assertion that fails on the trace, and that POL-RD-10(7) is confined to the partly corroborated case, which this is not.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02856", "EV-GPS-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-14", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No external traffic cause is available to the driver on this record. The bundle contains no traffic advisory for this trip: EV-ADVIS-02856-01 is admissibility MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and no payload, the artifact being minted only so the absence can be cited. I disclose that weight expressly, and cite the artifact for its absence. Because no advisory covers the trip window, the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run and any traffic assertion would carry no weight under POL-RD-08. I note that the driver's counterparty statement asserts a rider instruction, not a traffic cause, so nothing turns on POL-RD-13's priority rule here beyond confirming that no exoneration route is open.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02856-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no endpoint amendment to fall back on. POL-RD-05 requires a non-null pickup_amended_at or dropoff_amended_at and a stored amended_optimal_distance_km, and the trip_record shows amended_optimal_distance_km, amended_optimal_duration_min, pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at all null. The clause cannot be run, no substitute figure may be derived, and the baseline remains the booked optimal of 18.3 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nor is this a pooled trip. The vehicle type on the trip_record is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply, no matched-itinerary baseline displaces the booked optimal, and no co-rider collection distance is excluded from the excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare model on the fare_breakdown is METERED, so the distance-and-time refund route is open and POL-RD-11, which closes that route on upfront-quoted trips, has no application. The rider was billed per kilometre and per minute on a trip that was driven 5.49 km longer than the optimal route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-02 recomputation is arithmetic and it is not discretionary. ((3.80 + 0.75 x 18.3 + 0.28 x 24.7) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/tolls + 0 fixed surcharges + 0 waiting time - 0 promo = 25.241. The surge multiplier was read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, where it is 1.0, and not assumed absent, so no figure is doubled. The fare ledger's own derived money block confirms recomputed_fare of 25.2410.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Charged total was 31.13. Refund = 31.13 - 25.241 = 5.8890 before rounding, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05, which is 5.90. That is 18.9% of the charged total, well short of the 90% full-refund share POL-RD-02 sets, and well above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 5.90 against the rider's contested SGD 8.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no pass-through line to correct upwards or to double count. The fare_breakdown carries zero ERP and tolls, an empty erp_gantries array, an airport surcharge of 0.0 on a trip that neither originates at nor ends at an airport, and a waiting time fee of 0.0. The off-optimal-route ERP total is 0.00, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing to the POL-RD-02 figure and there is no billing-integrity defect to record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own profile does not raise the corroboration bar. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the four-claim trigger in POL-RD-08, so no corroboration beyond the gps_trace is required of this claim, and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated of 0 is not reached. I cite that field only for the POL-RD-08 test it names, as POL-GEN-01 requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The disputed charge was filed by the rider and the payment status on the fare ledger is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd of 0.0, so the refund runs to the rider. Under POL-GEN-03 a PARTIAL_REFUND returns part of the contested amount to the filing party and leaves the remainder of the present state standing; the rider should not be left carrying the SGD 5.90 attributable to 5.49 km of driving the optimal route did not require.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Taking the trace figure that governs under POL-RD-01 - gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 23.79 against the booked optimal of 18.3 - the excess is 5.49 km, or 30.0% of the optimal. That clears the establishment gates (0.8 km absolute and 20%) but falls short of BOTH materiality gates set by the same clause, 8.0 km absolute and 50%. This trip is therefore an established but NON-material deviation. Materiality is what opens the driver_profile consultation in POL-RD-06, and it is not reached here, so no material-deviation remedy and no uplift is available to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The repeat-deviation pattern test is not met and no profile-based amplification is open to the rider. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 408 - a rate of 0.00, below the 0.05 threshold, and the raw counter is below the 3 required. No pattern is ESTABLISHED, so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift in POL-RD-06(b) nor the driver-conduct referral in POL-RD-06(c) is available, and the rider's remedy stays on the POL-RD-02 arithmetic. Nor is this a case 'otherwise finely balanced' within POL-RD-06: the trace is unimpaired and unopposed, because the rider's detour request was not corroborated by it. POL-GEN-01 confines this claim to the two fields named above; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is a near-synonym and is not cited, and rating, acceptance_rate, cancellation_rate and active_region are context only.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's IMM request is genuinely on the file and the driver's account is not a bare assertion: chat message MSG-02856-001 was sent BY THE RIDER at 15:33:19, sixty seconds after the meter started, and carries a platform-resolved waypoint_hint for IMM, so limbs (a) to (c) of POL-RD-04 are met. The driver does not, however, claim exoneration under that clause, and candour requires the reason to be stated: the derived waypoint approach places the nearest fix 3088.34 m from IMM, so the 200 m corroboration test in POL-RD-04 fails, and under POL-RD-14 the instruction is taken as not having caused the measured excess and no distance is excluded. The request therefore neither excuses nor aggravates the deviation - it cannot be used to inflate the excess into a material or aggravated one, and the rider's remedy remains the plain POL-RD-01/POL-RD-02 figure on the trace as measured.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02856", "EV-GPS-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-14"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund on this METERED fare is arithmetic and cannot be inflated. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 18.3 + 0.28 x 24.7) x 1.0 surge_multiplier read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN + 0.80 platform fee = 25.241; refund = charged_total 31.13 - 25.241 = 5.889, rounded UP to SGD 5.90. That is above the 0.50 de minimis floor, so it is not a NO_ACTION, and it is 18.9% of charged_total, far below the 90% that would convert it into a FULL_REFUND. The driver's whole monetary exposure on this dispute is therefore SGD 5.90 - not the SGD 8.00 contested and not the SGD 31.13 charged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing is added on top of that figure under POL-RD-09. The fare carries no ERP lines and no airport surcharge: erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp is 0.00, airport_surcharge is 0.00, and this trip runs from Blk 12 Telok Blangah Cres to Blk 130 Bukit Batok West Ave 6, so it neither originates nor ends at an airport and no surcharge is properly chargeable. There is accordingly no unmatched gantry and no wrongly applied surcharge, no standalone billing-integrity correction arises, and the POL-RD-02 figure of SGD 5.90 is the entirety of what can move on this case.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

