consistent, and POL-RD-14 confines that trigger to the partly-corroborated case. There is no escalation on this point.\n\nNo other exoneration route is open. POL-RD-03 (road closure) needs a traffic advisory: none covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-02856-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, no payload) and no party asserted a traffic cause, so no traffic excuse is even in play. POL-RD-05 does not run: pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at, amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are all null, so the baseline stays the booked 18.3 km. POL-RD-12 does not run: the vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL. POL-RD-11 does not run: the fare model is METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE.\n\nThe refund is therefore the POL-RD-02 arithmetic on a METERED fare. The surge multiplier was read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, where it is 1.0, not assumed absent. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 18.3 + 0.28 x 24.7) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee = 24.441 + 0.80 = 25.241. Refund = charged_total 31.13 - 25.241 = 5.889, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 5.90. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis (so not NO_ACTION) and 18.9% of the charged total, far below the 90% that would convert it to a FULL_REFUND. The outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 5.90, not the SGD 8.00 contested and not the SGD 31.13 charged.\n\nNothing is added under POL-RD-09. The fare carries no ERP lines (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00), no airport surcharge (0.00, and the trip neither originates nor ends at an airport), and no waiting-time fee. There is no unmatched gantry and no wrongly applied surcharge, so no billing-integrity finding and no referral arises. Driver compensation under POL-RD-04 does not arise either: the rider was billed 23.8 km against a 23.79 km trace, a shortfall of well under the 1.0 km threshold.\n\nThe trace is clean for POL-RD-07 purposes: 187 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, an empty gaps array and a max_gap_sec of 0.0, so no limb (a) to (c) is met and no corroboration requirement or POL-RD-10(3) escalation is engaged. Trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (TRP-02856), timestamps do not conflict, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires. My confidence rests on artifacts all at weight_multiplier 1.0 (EV-GPS-02856, EV-TRIP-02856, EV-FARE-02856, EV-CHAT-02856), so the cap is 1.0; the missing advisory (weight 0.0) carries no deciding fact and does not lower it. The one rider claim citing that absent artifact was discarded at the citation stage for not naming its issue code. My confidence of 0.90 is above the 0.70 floor, so the case does not escalate.\n\nThe monetary effect of SGD 5.90 is at or below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this provisional ruling may be executed on issue; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04.",
